      "side": 0,
      "message": "To clarify further, I have no idea about this vndk/sphal business. I just know that without linking a list of libs like `linkDriverNamespaceLocked` does, loading the library as \"isolated\" fails with errors like `dlopen_ext(\"libEGL_angle.so\") failed: dlopen failed: library \"libdl.so\" not found`. So we can\u0027t just return early like we did before with \"shared isolated\" dlopen. Now whether it is correct to just remove this block or not, I don\u0027t know. I only know that it worked this way on cuttlefish.",
